From: hashtagbasit
Subject: drm/msm: map submitqueue priorities onto HIGH..LOW in order

msm_gpu_convert_priority() still inverts the per-ring priority from before
drm_sched made lower enum values higher priority, so each ring's lowest
userspace priority became DRM_SCHED_PRIORITY_KERNEL. A game's Turnip queue
then outranked Steam's GL clients (Xwayland, the Steam UI, mangoapp) on the
same ring and starved them while the game kept the GPU busy: Quick Access
not drawn, the UI freezing and then catching up. Map 0..2 onto HIGH..LOW and
index the entity array from HIGH. VM_BIND queues keep KERNEL. Same issue
ArmadaOS found.

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.h
@@ -531,8 +531,8 @@
  * is mapped to ring nr and scheduler priority as such:
  *
  *   ring_nr    = userspace_prio / NR_SCHED_PRIORITIES
- *   sched_prio = NR_SCHED_PRIORITIES -
- *                (userspace_prio % NR_SCHED_PRIORITIES) - 1
+ *   sched_prio = DRM_SCHED_PRIORITY_HIGH +
+ *                (userspace_prio % NR_SCHED_PRIORITIES)
  *
  * This allows generations without preemption (nr_rings==1) to have some
  * amount of prioritization, and provides more priority levels for gens
@@ -547,10 +547,16 @@
 
 	rn = div_u64_rem(prio, NR_SCHED_PRIORITIES, &sp);
 
-	/* invert sched priority to map to higher-numeric-is-higher-
-	 * priority convention
+	/*
+	 * Lower userspace values are higher priority, and so are lower
+	 * drm_sched_priority values: map 0..2 onto HIGH..LOW in order. The old
+	 * inversion (from before drm_sched flipped its enum) put each ring's
+	 * lowest userspace priority at KERNEL, so a game's Turnip queue
+	 * outranked Steam's GL clients (Xwayland, the Steam UI, mangoapp) and
+	 * starved them while the game kept the GPU busy. KERNEL stays with the
+	 * VM_BIND queues.
 	 */
-	sp = NR_SCHED_PRIORITIES - sp - 1;
+	sp += DRM_SCHED_PRIORITY_HIGH;
 
 	if (rn >= gpu->nr_rings)
 		return -EINVAL;
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_submitqueue.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_submitqueue.c
@@ -137,7 +137,8 @@
 		 unsigned ring_nr, enum drm_sched_priority sched_prio)
 {
 	static DEFINE_MUTEX(entity_lock);
-	unsigned idx = (ring_nr * NR_SCHED_PRIORITIES) + sched_prio;
+	unsigned idx = (ring_nr * NR_SCHED_PRIORITIES) +
+		       (sched_prio - DRM_SCHED_PRIORITY_HIGH);
 
 	/* We should have already validated that the requested priority is
 	 * valid by the time we get here.
